{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/104453-developers-specific-sources-of-lunar-inspiration","id":104453,"title":"[Developers] Specific sources of Lunar inspiration?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-02T17:24:59-07:00","id":104453,"title":"[Developers] Specific sources of Lunar inspiration?","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">We prefer mythic shapeshifters and primal gods to John Carpenter's THE THING.<br /> <br /> &quot;Werewolf-inspired Exalted&quot; is arguably an even richer concept-mine than &quot;Frankenstein-inspired Exalted.&quot; [1] Taking the oWoD's particular interpretation of werewolves as both a solid starting point and a limiter for exploring the concept is a terrible mistake, though.<br /> <br /> [1] Particularly when you expand &quot;Frankenstein&quot; to &quot;all tales of created life or unnatural outcasts are fair game for inspiration,&quot; and particularly when you expand &quot;werewolf&quot; to &quot;all tales of bestial dualism, and all shapeshifting folklore of any kind.&quot; I mean, hardly anyone in America has ever even heard of them, but I could riff on African werehyena legends alone pretty much forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you point us in the direction of the particular legends, myths and characters that you have chosen for your Lunar Exalted inspiration? Son Goku and Hanuman are easily found everywhere on the internet, but what about these werehyenas? And which &quot;primal gods&quot;?<br /> <br /> <br /> Any characters from more modern forms of media would also be appreciated. John's already on record as rejecting Alex Mercer (<i>[Prototype]</i>), the T-1000 (<i>Terminator: Judgment Day</i>), Twelve (<i>Street Fighter</i>), Reed Richards (<i>Fantastic Four</i>) and Mystique (<i>X-Men</i>).<br /> <br /> I figure Wolverine, Sabertooth, and Beastboy (<i>Teen Titans</i>) are still applicable, as it would be pretty hard to avoid any of them. Arakune (<i>BlazBlue</i>) is basically a giant spider, if practically made of slime and bones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T17:45:13-07:00","id":104478,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/ee/Werewolf_-_The_Apocalypse_cover.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">The obvious one.</a><br /> <br /> Cheetah* would be a good Lunar to Wonder Woman's Solar. She's not only a super-powered catperson but an aristocrat and archeologist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 04-02-2014, 08:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T11:53:43-07:00","id":105708,"title":"","content":"Reminds me of the Black Panther, who is empowered by a tribal panther god. Or would he make a better Solar?<br /> <br /> Also, Bigwig!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T11:56:32-07:00","id":105711,"title":"","content":"T'Challah is an Ochilike. Possibly an Exigent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T12:23:04-07:00","id":105738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/104453-developers-specific-sources-of-lunar-inspiration#post104453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Son Goku and Hanuman are easily found everywhere on the internet, but what about these werehyenas?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Werehyena#African_cultures\" target=\"_blank\">Here's the short version</a>. It's pretty standard witch-slash-skinwalker stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T13:22:09-07:00","id":105785,"title":"","content":"<i>I have a question.<br /> Now, the new theme of the Lunars is the Mythical Monster, Your Hydra's, your Nemean Lions, Your Spider-themed Prostitute Yokai (yes, those are a thing), and personally, I really like that.<br /> But do creatures like Ogres, Giants and Cyclopses count towards this group as well?</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T13:31:20-07:00","id":105791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/104453-developers-specific-sources-of-lunar-inspiration?p=105785#post105785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>I have a question.<br /> Now, the new theme of the Lunars is the Mythical Monster, Your Hydra's, your Nemean Lions, Your Spider-themed Prostitute Yokai (yes, those are a thing), and personally, I really like that.<br /> But do creatures like Ogres, Giants and Cyclopses count towards this group as well?</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, one of the example Tell suggestions in 1e was having a single cyclops eye, so some of them could be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T14:11:38-07:00","id":105814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/104453-developers-specific-sources-of-lunar-inspiration?p=105708#post105708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reminds me of the Black Panther, who is empowered by a tribal panther god. Or would he make a better Solar?<br /> <br /> Also, Bigwig!</div> </div> </div> </div>T'Challa could be both. Thematically speaking he's both totemic and also an exemplar of arete, are Lunar and Solar concepts respectively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T14:18:34-07:00","id":105820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/104453-developers-specific-sources-of-lunar-inspiration?p=105738#post105738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Werehyena#African_cultures\" target=\"_blank\">Here's the short version</a>. It's pretty standard witch-slash-skinwalker stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>In the Kanuri language of the former Bornu Empire in the Lake Chad region, werehyenas are referred to as bultungin which translates into &quot;I change myself into a hyena&quot;.[2] It was once traditionally believed that one or two of the villages in the region was populated entirely by werehyenas,[1] such as Kabultiloa.[3]<br /> <br /> In Ethiopia, it is traditionally believed that every blacksmith, whose trade is hereditary, is really a wizard or witch with the power to change into a hyena. These blacksmith werehyenas are believed to rob graves at midnight and are referred to as bouda[1] (also spelled buda).[2][4] They are viewed with suspicion by most countrymen. Belief in the bouda is also present in Sudan, Tanzania and Morocco where some among the Berber people regard the bouda as a man or woman who nightly turns into a hyena and resumes human shape at dawn.[1] Many Ethiopian Christians characterize Ethiopian Jews as being bouda, accusing them of unearthing Christian corpses and consuming them; the commonality of blacksmithing as a traditional profession for Jewish men in Ethiopia may be a reason for the connection between the two beliefs.[4]</i><br /> <br /> Eheh... this is terrible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T18:57:14-07:00","id":105967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/104453-developers-specific-sources-of-lunar-inspiration?p=105708#post105708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reminds me of the Black Panther, who is empowered by a tribal panther god. Or would he make a better Solar?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. The way Black Panther gets written lately, he strikes me as someone who'd be better represented as a Solar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T06:35:25-07:00","id":106240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/104453-developers-specific-sources-of-lunar-inspiration?p=105814#post105814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> T'Challa could be both. Thematically speaking he's both totemic and also an exemplar of arete, are Lunar and Solar concepts respectively.</div> </div> </div> </div>Double-Exaltation, feh! As Mnemon has showed us, the <i>true</i> power can only be reached by one who wields <i>three</i> Exaltations! :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T06:42:01-07:00","id":106246,"title":"","content":"What make Black Panther a Lunar aside from having animal name in his codename and wearing an animal suite ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T07:11:17-07:00","id":106256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/104453-developers-specific-sources-of-lunar-inspiration?p=105785#post105785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>I have a question.<br /> Now, the new theme of the Lunars is the Mythical Monster, Your Hydra's, your Nemean Lions, Your Spider-themed Prostitute Yokai (yes, those are a thing), and personally, I really like that.<br /> But do creatures like Ogres, Giants and Cyclopses count towards this group as well?</i></div> </div> </div> </div>There's a reason No Moons are known as Ogres in popular imagination (the way Dawns are known as Forsaken, Changing Moons are known as Tricksters, etc).<br /> Remember the Ogre from the original Puss-in-boots story? He's a powerful sorcerer, lives in a castle, turns into a lion, and turns into a mouse (and then Puss eats him).<br /> The giants of Welsh legend probably fit too, with all their magical stuff... to a limit.<br /> I'd say the more humanoid monsters should probably be less of an influence. I certainly wouldn't mind seeing Lunars being able to make themselves bigger though.<br /> <br /> The magical animals of Chinese and Japanese legend should definitely be a major influence. Snakes, foxes, etc, that live for thousands of years and gain enlightenment, so they can shapechange into humans and perhaps other things. Many of them are trickster spirits. Selkies maybe as well. The monster in the forest that takes human form to lure people in, then slaughter them.<br /> Although of course, while Lunars take the form of monsters, they're humans as well, so it's a kind of inversion.<br /> <br /> There are a fair few Trickster-shapechanger archetypes as well. Coyote, Loki, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T07:21:38-07:00","id":106259,"title":"","content":"Anansi, like Loki, is another shapeshifting trickster God, so a good inspiration for Changing Moons.<br /> <br /> You'll notice most of these are gods, rather than the mythical beasts that others were suggesting.<br /> <br /> The issue with mythical beasts is that they're fine for Full Moons, but rather too physical to cover all bases. Full Moons had the best charms in 2nd and 1st ed, followed by Changing Moons, with No Moons a rather paltry 3rd (actually, in 1st ed I don't think Changing Moons were that great either, but I only read the 1st ed Lunar charms briefly, as I never played 1st ed).<br /> I don't want to see that situation repeated, with the physical attributes getting all the best charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T08:26:08-07:00","id":106284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/104453-developers-specific-sources-of-lunar-inspiration?p=105814#post105814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">T'Challa could be both. Thematically speaking he's both totemic and also an exemplar of arete, are Lunar and Solar concepts respectively.</div> </div> </div> </div>He could be either, but not both.<br /> <br /> As a Solar, he could have a panther as his anima icon (totem), and his player can design him to fit with the themes of that totem, but that doesn't mean it needs to be a totem to the extent that the Lunar Exalted take the concept.<br /> <br /> As a Lunar, he could approach arete to the extent that Lunars can, if not to the extent that a Solar could.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T08:50:12-07:00","id":106302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/104453-developers-specific-sources-of-lunar-inspiration?p=106256#post106256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a reason No Moons are known as Ogres in popular imagination (the way Dawns are known as Forsaken, Changing Moons are known as Tricksters, etc).<br /> Remember the Ogre from the original Puss-in-boots story? He's a powerful sorcerer, lives in a castle, turns into a lion, and turns into a mouse (and then Puss eats him).<br /> The giants of Welsh legend probably fit too, with all their magical stuff... to a limit.<br /> I'd say the more humanoid monsters should probably be less of an influence. I certainly wouldn't mind seeing Lunars being able to make themselves bigger though.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are plenty of things that kind of skirt the border between divine beast and monstrous humanoid. On the one hand, you have things like the supposed connection between cyclopes and elephants, and on the other you have oni, who are bestial despite being humanoid and serve double duty as monstrous bringers of calamity and fierce guardian spirits.<br /> <br /> As for &quot;primal gods,&quot; there is Set, god of storms, violence, and foreigners, and guardian of the sun; Tezcatlipoca, <i>teotl</i> of sorcery and beauty and night and chaos, among so many other things; Dionysus, outsider god of wine and ecstatic revelation; Kali, terrible, beloved mother goddess, and destroyer of evil; Gozu-Tenn\u014d, fierce lord of disease and benevolent protector <i>from</i> disease; et cetera, et cetera.<br /> And these are just the famous ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T09:06:49-07:00","id":106311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/104453-developers-specific-sources-of-lunar-inspiration?p=106259#post106259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anansi, like Loki, is another shapeshifting trickster God, so a good inspiration for Changing Moons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Studying how he tricked others led me to deconstruct the various skills that tricksters use to fool people (even the people who should know better), but the stories themselves provided no <i>particular</i> feat that seemed like a Lunar Charm to me. Or perhaps I should say, none of his feats seemed to inspire a <i>spectacular</i> Lunar Charm.<br /> <br /> Not in the way that, for instance, Hanuman growing into a giant could be a Charm or Knack, or how having physical representations of Rama and Sita (the couple whom he loved above all) inside of his flesh-and-blood heart could be a Charm.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You'll notice most of these are gods, rather than the mythical beasts that others were suggesting.<br /> <br /> The issue with mythical beasts is that they're fine for Full Moons, but rather too physical to cover all bases. Full Moons had the best charms in 2nd and 1st ed, followed by Changing Moons, with No Moons a rather paltry 3rd (actually, in 1st ed I don't think Changing Moons were that great either, but I only read the 1st ed Lunar charms briefly, as I never played 1st ed).<br /> I don't want to see that situation repeated, with the physical attributes getting all the best charms. </div> </div> </div>+1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T11:42:34-07:00","id":106415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/104453-developers-specific-sources-of-lunar-inspiration?p=106259#post106259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue with mythical beasts is that they're fine for Full Moons, but rather too physical to cover all bases. Full Moons had the best charms in 2nd and 1st ed, followed by Changing Moons, with No Moons a rather paltry 3rd (actually, in 1st ed I don't think Changing Moons were that great either, but I only read the 1st ed Lunar charms briefly, as I never played 1st ed).<br /> I don't want to see that situation repeated, with the physical attributes getting all the best charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't look like that's going to happen:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">One commonality is that shapeshifting remains a strong tool, and that Lunars draw extreme power from their physicality, be it from their intense sexuality, their furious / terrifying might, or <u>their ability to shape their reptilian hindbrains to a higher form, making insights of a higher form, seeing with ancient eyes the truths of another age.</u> They are tremendously physical characters and this is something to be proud of, not to run away from.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something to be considered with respect to the recurring arguments over Lunar intelligence, by the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 04-05-2014, 02:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T12:08:47-07:00","id":106432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/104453-developers-specific-sources-of-lunar-inspiration?p=106415#post106415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Doesn't look like that's going to happen:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Something to be considered with respect to the recurring arguments over Lunar intelligence, by the way.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Triune_brain#Status_of_the_model\" target=\"_blank\">Or perhaps not.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T12:16:56-07:00","id":106439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/104453-developers-specific-sources-of-lunar-inspiration?p=106302#post106302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for &quot;primal gods,&quot; there is Set, god of storms, violence, and foreigners, and guardian of the sun; Tezcatlipoca, <i>teotl</i> of sorcery and beauty and night and chaos, among so many other things; <b>Dionysus, outsider god of wine and ecstatic revelation; </b>Kali, terrible, beloved mother goddess, and destroyer of evil; Gozu-Tenn\u014d, fierce lord of disease and benevolent protector <i>from</i> disease; et cetera, et cetera.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget Pan, a figure so strange to the point of being out of place in his mythology that some scholars think he may be a holdover from a much earlier religion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 04-05-2014, 03:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T12:26:09-07:00","id":106441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/104453-developers-specific-sources-of-lunar-inspiration?p=106432#post106432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Triune_brain#Status_of_the_model\" target=\"_blank\">Or perhaps not.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>It's funny to think that a year from now when their Charms are out, you're going to be pointing to Wikipedia articles to prove they don't do what they say they do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 04-05-2014, 03:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T13:26:33-07:00","id":106479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/104453-developers-specific-sources-of-lunar-inspiration?p=106441#post106441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's funny to think that a year from now when their Charms are out, you're going to be pointing to Wikipedia articles to prove they don't do what they say they do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just a year? Wow, now <i>that</i> is funny.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T14:16:56-07:00","id":106509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/104453-developers-specific-sources-of-lunar-inspiration?p=106479#post106479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a year? Wow, now <i>that</i> is funny.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we haven't seen any spoiled or leaked charms, and we don't have a situation like in 2nd Edition when the Storyteller's Companion contained Lunar charms for use in games a year before the actual Lunars rulebook was published, I'm guessing there will at least be a lot more statements like the one above. So start planning how you're going to use Wikipedia to argue against them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T14:31:10-07:00","id":106522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/104453-developers-specific-sources-of-lunar-inspiration?p=106432#post106432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Triune_brain#Status_of_the_model\" target=\"_blank\">Or perhaps not.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>You say that as though it was the only possible interpretation.<br /> Also, you're interpreting it in a very narrow way. As someone that works with neural networks and AI, let me tell ya: having more properly structured neurons makes a pretty big difference.<br /> The example basically only talks about modding your neural structure ( with evolutionary terms sprinkled in for fluff) which can and regularly does provide concrete results. Just because some research seems to suggest that specific parts of the brain don't work the way we thought they did, doesn't mean that magically restructuring your neural architecture can't and doesn't give results.<br /> <br /> It's like saying that having a stroke doesn't have much short-term baring on your cognitive faculties.<br /> \u200b<br /> Also, in a game where physics is literally run by ninja-wizards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":"ninja-wizards 04-05-2014, 05:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T14:50:11-07:00","id":106539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/104453-developers-specific-sources-of-lunar-inspiration?p=106522#post106522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You say that as though it was the only possible interpretation.<br /> Also, you're interpreting it in a very narrow way. As someone that works with neural networks and AI, let me tell ya: having more properly structured neurons makes a pretty big difference.<br /> The example basically only talks about modding your neural structure ( with evolutionary terms sprinkled in for fluff) which can and regularly does provide concrete results. Just because some research seems to suggest that specific parts of the brain don't work the way we thought they did, doesn't mean that magically restructuring your neural architecture can't and doesn't give results.</div> </div> </div> </div>The phrasing of the quote doesn't really cite that as a reason. Beyond that, altering neural architecture as a method of working a Charm can cross over into scifi territory rather quickly, which is something that they were supposedly cutting back on, what with striking the term 'magitech' from the setting. It's difficult to uphold the direction of going for mythic resonance if you then decide that you're going to shoot for something else entirely as well. There's little mythic resonance in a mistake of terminology that someone made back in the 60s because they had never actually looked at a sauropsidian brain closely before.<br /> <br /> Conversely, pulp adventure stories were big into pineal eyes. i'm surprised that nothing about them has shown up in the past 13 years. They ought to be entrenched, like those Charles R. Knight dinosaurs that exist alongside modern conceptions of the same in the setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's like saying that having a stroke doesn't have much short-term baring on your cognitive faculties. </div> </div> </div>Reptiles have hind, mid and forebrains, incidentally.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, in a game where physics is literally run by wizards. </div> </div> </div>This meme needs to die. The gods don't uphold causality, unless those gods are the Maidens and they're taking time out of the Jade Pleasure Dome to maintain it personally like they used to (which they really just don't do anymore). Many gods can influence it, but it goes on without them. They just make reports out of what they find, if they can even be bothered to do that. It's a good thing that Creation doesn't rely on them, in fact, because they usually spend whole weeks at parties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T15:05:12-07:00","id":106548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/104453-developers-specific-sources-of-lunar-inspiration?p=106432#post106432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Triune_brain#Status_of_the_model\" target=\"_blank\">Or perhaps not.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Something doesn't have to be factual for Lunars to draw from it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T15:19:26-07:00","id":106556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/104453-developers-specific-sources-of-lunar-inspiration?p=106539#post106539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The phrasing of the quote doesn't really cite that as a reason. Beyond that, altering neural architecture as a method of working a Charm can cross over into scifi territory rather quickly, which is something that they were supposedly cutting back on, what with striking the term 'magitech' from the setting. It's difficult to uphold the direction of going for mythic resonance if you then decide that you're going to shoot for something else entirely as well. There's little mythic resonance in a mistake of terminology that someone made back in the 60s because they had never actually looked at a sauropsidian brain closely before.<br /> <br /> Conversely, pulp adventure stories were big into pineal eyes. i'm surprised that nothing about them has shown up in the past 13 years. They ought to be entrenched, like those Charles R. Knight dinosaurs that exist alongside modern conceptions of the same in the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, John Carter or Mars is technically sci-fi, and I'd tend to say that it fits Lunars rather well :P<br /> That aside, it's a valid complaint that it can slide out of theme pretty easily from there, but at the same time if they <i>are</i> going for physicality, and want to have intelligence and wits charms that actually fit that theme, I find it perfectly valid to get lunars to grow or &quot;uplift&quot; their brains (or parts thereof).<br /> <br /> And even then, the quote only said uplifting parts of their brains and didn't specifically reference any research. In this context &quot;uplifting&quot; can simply be taken to mean &quot;more complex&quot;, and that just basically means more neurons, that you could dedicate to anything you like, because magic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This meme needs to die. The gods don't uphold causality, unless those gods are the Maidens and they're taking time out of the Jade Pleasure Dome to maintain it personally like they used to (which they really just don't do anymore). Many gods can influence it, but it goes on without them. They just make reports out of what they find, if they can even be bothered to do that. It's a good thing that Creation doesn't rely on them, in fact, because they usually spend whole weeks at parties. </div> </div> </div>Getting stuck on &quot;Lunar magic can't work like that because the real world doesn't work like that&quot; ignores the fact that the real world also doesn't work on motes, or have titans, or isn't surrounded by a sea of chaos. Should those things <i>also</i> work as they do in the real world? Lunar charms can simply work <i>because magic</i>, and the manifestation of that magic is physicality.<br /> <br /> And hell, it could be argued that since the inspirations that are going into the Lunars are from pre-60s, it doesn't go out-of-theme to base some powers on the preconceptions about biology that fantasy writers had around that time.<br /> <br /> <b>TLDR: </b>what hippokrene said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 04-05-2014, 06:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T15:37:36-07:00","id":106564,"title":"","content":"Besides which, for all you know Lunars actually <i>can</i> have reptilian hindbrains. So there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T15:55:07-07:00","id":106579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/104453-developers-specific-sources-of-lunar-inspiration?p=106479#post106479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just a year? Wow, now <i>that</i> is funny.</div> </div> </div> </div>If by &quot;funny&quot; you mean &quot;I'm laughing to contain my tears&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T16:03:57-07:00","id":106585,"title":"","content":"I have problems with the physicality approach to lunars. To clarify, I don't have a problem with the concept or its emphasis, I am worried about it being overemphasized or misunderstood. Lunars already are pigeonholed as mostly physical if only because finding suitable themes for their mental and social charms is problematic. I think John is right in not laying that problem at the feet of physicality, but I've already seen people misinterpret his statement to mean that physicality is the primary nature of lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T21:00:05-07:00","id":106700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/104453-developers-specific-sources-of-lunar-inspiration?p=106585#post106585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have problems with the physicality approach to lunars. To clarify, I don't have a problem with the concept or its emphasis, I am worried about it being overemphasized or misunderstood. Lunars already are pigeonholed as mostly physical if only because finding suitable themes for their mental and social charms is problematic. I think John is right in not laying that problem at the feet of physicality, but I've already seen people misinterpret his statement to mean that physicality is the primary nature of lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>He means physicality in a real visceral way, just in a violence capacity. No illusions happening, that fear is very real as if that monster coming to eat your head than was once your mistress.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T22:35:07-07:00","id":106738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/104453-developers-specific-sources-of-lunar-inspiration?p=106700#post106700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He means physicality in a real visceral way, just in a violence capacity. No illusions happening, that fear is very real as if that monster coming to eat your head than was once your mistress.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm reminded, for whatever reason, of the realization I had about the common element of Demon: the Descent's demonic forms (summarized roughly as &quot;your demonic form is not a hologram&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T00:54:20-07:00","id":106777,"title":"","content":"I'd probably be okay with such a physical approach, as long as there are enough social and, more importantly, mental charms.<br /> It seems a little limiting though, in terms of inspiring charms, so I'm worried we'll once again have a situation where No Moons are vastly eclipsed by Full Moons, rather than just being different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T04:51:43-07:00","id":106831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/104453-developers-specific-sources-of-lunar-inspiration?p=106700#post106700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He means physicality in a real visceral way, just in a violence capacity. No illusions happening, that fear is very real as if that monster coming to eat your head than was once your mistress.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know what he means, I still have a problem with the idea for the reasons I said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T10:37:08-07:00","id":106969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/104453-developers-specific-sources-of-lunar-inspiration?p=106700#post106700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He means physicality in a real visceral way, just in a violence capacity. No illusions happening, that fear is very real as if that monster coming to eat your head than was once your mistress.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that this <i>doesn't</i> really work outside of physical Charms, which we have already established are the predominant Charm type for Lunar Exalted. Cool, I can reorganize my brain to be smarter-er!... But how does that actually get applied in the context of design? Similarly, are we just supposed to turn Lunar social Charms into flesh-sculpting and pheromones? Because that's interesting for maybe five Charms, and then you need to think up something else.<br /> <br /> Lunars have a lot more space to grow in if you take it from outside the physical space- illusion, mystery, madness, rage, chaos, insight and prophecy are all things traditionally associated with the moon, most of which don't fit neatly into a &quot;physical&quot; theme and most of which I'd like to see Lunars explore more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;We do not quit playing because we grow old, we grow old because we quit playing.&quot; - Oliver Wendell Holmes","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/283-mrinsecure","name":"MrInsecure","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T18:38:22-07:00","id":119490,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, primal gods...<br /> <br /> Sekhmet, lioness-headed Egyptian god of war, fire and vengeance, Before Whom Evil Trembles, Mistress of Dread, Lady of Slaughter, She Who Mauls, Ra's selected source of retribution against treacherous humanity who then had to be rendered stone drink when her blood lust raged out of control and threatened to destroy all humans (although she's a friendly and placid drunk).<br /> <br /> I've also got something of a mind towards the Morrigan, shapeshifting haunter of battlefields, crafty and a bitter fighter, contributes pursuit, subduing and destruction to war, who sought to torment C\u00fa Chulainn in the shape of eel and crow and wolf and cow, a sexual creature who fought the enemy of gods by taking the blood of his heart and the kidneys of his valour and depositing handfuls of them in the river.<br /> <br /> I kind of think a god might be &quot;primal&quot; when it appears to be a rather visceral, if not violent, creature, ones immersed in flesh and the moment, ones who seem to lack a lot of the pretensions of godlyness, possibly even to the point of being subversions of their native mythology, viewed as fearsome beings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T19:21:19-07:00","id":119510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/104453-developers-specific-sources-of-lunar-inspiration?p=105738#post105738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Werehyena#African_cultures\" target=\"_blank\">Here's the short version</a>. It's pretty standard witch-slash-skinwalker stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>I already searched Wikipedia. It doesn't turn up any specific stories or legends, such as Holden seems to refer. The sparse article certainly doesn't seem to be something someone &quot;could riff off of forever&quot;.<br /> <br /> Searching for Anansi turns up gobs of websites other than Wikipedia, whereas &quot;Werehyena&quot; gets a lot of hits apparently based more on DnD, the shared mythology of Otherkin and furry communities, and modern ideas of werewolves rather than anything from Africa.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T19:33:27-07:00","id":119514,"title":"","content":"So would Sun Wukong be a Lunar or a Solar beastman?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T19:45:16-07:00","id":119519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/104453-developers-specific-sources-of-lunar-inspiration?p=119514#post119514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So would Sun Wukong be a Lunar or a Solar beastman?</div> </div> </div> </div>Either.<br /> <br /> Reading a synopsis of his life, any ability you couldn't do with a Solar Charm is really incidental. Commanding wind and water, or spawning clones and turning into objects, are things a Dawn Caste Solar monkey beastman could do with Sorcery, and possibly martial arts and Evocations.<br /> <br /> <br /> But speaking of the ability to spawn clones, I hope there's a middle ground between &quot;become a country-choking swarm&quot; and &quot;become Godzilla&quot;. Like, &quot;become a city-swarming horde of elephant-sized wolves.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T19:59:29-07:00","id":119521,"title":"","content":"The main thing that favors the Lunar interpretation instead of Solar beastman are the transformations: he becomes a giant, grows multiple arms, changes his appearance, turns into a fly, various objects and so on. He also often is shown to have a Tell, being unable to hide his tail when transforming into other people","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T23:59:20-07:00","id":119601,"title":"","content":"Sun Wukong can do pretty much anything power wise so that's not helpful<br /> <br /> Theme wise he's a trickster and wind up merchant who takes the piss out of the Gods, loses his temper and is very fickle<br /> <br /> So I'd say more fitting with the Lunar, though like most heroic characters, he could be either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T12:39:31-07:00","id":119897,"title":"","content":"Anyone who's ever been changed in some manner by getting some monster's blood all over them. That's a suitable inspiration there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T14:22:29-07:00","id":119964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God_of_Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/104453-developers-specific-sources-of-lunar-inspiration?p=119897#post119897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone who's ever been changed in some manner by getting some monster's blood all over them. That's a suitable inspiration there.</div> </div> </div> </div> So, Axe Cop then?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T17:31:04-07:00","id":120055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/104453-developers-specific-sources-of-lunar-inspiration?p=119601#post119601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sun Wukong can do pretty much anything power wise so that's not helpful<br /> <br /> Theme wise he's a trickster and wind up merchant who takes the piss out of the Gods, loses his temper and is very fickle<br /> <br /> So I'd say more fitting with the Lunar, though like most heroic characters, he could be either.</div> </div> </div> </div>He is also often cited as an example of how having &quot;companion&quot; as your archetype can still be cool and still allow you to be the main character of your story.<br /> <br /> (Of course he's like bazillion times more powerful than Xuanzang, which isn't always an option for Lunars, but having different focuses works for that if you eg. picture Xuanzang as a socialize / medicine-focused character.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}